  "summary_en": "Florida statute section 316.2071 allows personal delivery devices and mobile carriers to operate on sidewalks and crosswalks with pedestrian rights and duties. It sets equipment, identification, operator monitoring and prohibition rules, and requires operators to carry at least $100,000 general liability insurance.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Devices may operate on sidewalks and crosswalks with pedestrian rights and duties, yielding to pedestrians",
   "Must obey signals, display unique ID plate with operator contact, and have a braking system",
   "Operator must actively control or monitor the device; mobile carrier owner within 25 feet",
   "Prohibited from carrying hazardous materials or, for mobile carriers, persons or animals",
   "Owners must maintain at least $100,000 general liability insurance"
